+{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_e62L5LDrZi80aoGJu1BeygoO","content":"1\t# D.110c-0b0 GREEN ledger\n2\t\n3\t- Starting source commit: `798489fdef5fc3a6d774ecb2ccc075205e00e254`\n4\t- Starting tree: `1c923fc1d67e537738384e214902a30f7bb80048`\n5\t- Scope: application/account room-head authority plumbing for the genuine first creator handoff, exact hot/cold expected-head enforcement, retained product/test adaptation, and no protocol/wire/dependency change.\n6\t- No D.110a invocation, preflight, retained campaign, long multi-epoch run, or collaboration subagent ran.\n7\t\n8\t## Executable results\n9\t\n10\t- The frozen focused command selected one test in one file. Its test semantics passed 1/1 with JSON `success:true`, zero failed, and zero pending. The shell status was 1 solely because the command inherited the repository-wide 70% coverage gate (observed 16.36%); it was not rerun. Reporter SHA-256: `3d8f2391d4ba1059bca42eb86a0dfc330b92563fcdede49415935a6c5320386d`.\n11\t- The first exact nine-file retained run passed 95/97. Its two failures were stale source-governance expectations for the former direct commit consumer and byte-identical chat owner, not runtime semantics. Reporter SHA-256: `4fc71562d38b89534818137ada268f06318da41974a1231d83c7362607f80ff4`.\n12\t- Those test-only expectations were corrected in one batch. The final retained run passed 97/97 across 20 suites, with zero failures or pending tests. Reporter SHA-256: `65b6c35141885ecc5e8ab0fe6b7c7dc944325a8249ffdccdc850e422ee7abb8f`.\n13\t- The first three-engine browser product run exposed `intent-unavailable` in all engines. Cause: the test instrumentation intercepted verification from fresh source while the new stage/recovery subpaths resolved through built package artifacts, creating a second process-local WeakMap custody realm. The harness now intercepts stage and recovery through the same source realm. Failed reporter SHA-256: `9f301c7deb41e88c9b14ef600c0c9cebadaa198185af41d13f4e9c5bf51f1d70`.\n14\t- The next browser run passed the hot and established-reopen rows but found one stale creator epoch-one rejoin call that omitted the newly mandatory room head. Failed reporter SHA-256: `2e868495c9ed3e1512dc8b3bdcde29ab09c6d78d092686568f81bda50903cdc0`.\n15\t- After that fixture-only correction, the complete product browser gate passed 24/24 in Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit, with zero skipped, unexpected, or flaky results. Reporter SHA-256: `56a53de0ee5c5c051b245f201ee97d031e64cea295189cb57bc7835cd7308b18`.\n16\t\n17\t## Static and build gates\n18\t\n19\t- `pnpm --filter @ts-drp/node exec tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.build.json`: pass.\n20\t- `pnpm --filter @ts-drp/example-v3-room typecheck`: pass.\n21\t- `pnpm --filter ts-drp-example-v3-chat typecheck`: pass.\n22\t- `node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit -p tests/fixtures/phase-3a1b-p3/tsconfig.test.json`: pass.\n23\t- Affected Node, v3-room, and v3-chat builds: pass.\n24\t- Exact changed-owner ESLint and Prettier: pass.\n25\t- The first whole-plan Prettier check exhausted Node's default heap on the 93,000-line plan. The same read-only formatter check passed with `NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=8192`; no product/test memory limit changed.\n26\t- `git diff --check`: pass.\n27\t- Corrected source audit: pass; SHA-256 `b338d1b840e0086f2500a3dbf6b48e9f17f1d9d3ce0ca0b0e2c394b7b52c443e`.\n28\t- The first source audit used the faulty literal `expectedRoomHead:` count. It was corrected to count the two actual capture and equality checks; the diagnostic mistake is not a code failure.\n29\t- Root `package.json` and `pnpm-lock.yaml` retain their frozen hashes. No protocol-v3, registry, wire, schema, dependency, threshold, workload, or long-run path changed.\n30\t\n31\t## Owner identities\n32\t\n33\t- `examples/v3-room/src/index.ts`: `3a6057ef8e11c7b5ce00c74180b3f2740cc79ec4dbc262fd67f8555239956d73`\n34\t- `examples/v3-chat/src/index.ts`: `ede864e4b7c10ebd578f7ddec47868ffe864e37991f4f07c4cb28e9795c17b67`\n35\t- `packages/node/src/creator-adoption-activate.ts`: `a0de90e3d74177ac505da9e5f5c94985642cb585eecfa9e6d336f0745a0bfffe`\n36\t- `packages/node/src/internal/creator-room-head.ts`: `f9cd1ab69e9f7deba0872894e4df4b8bfd5687bd7096e3ace8c217cf7ac9b9fc`\n37\t- `packages/node/src/internal/creator-successor-live.ts`: `41df016f2dbb5b2681657930b3cf5341b253ff961ae6871cc892eb4c2f6023fd`\n38\t- focused owner: `5f65a4d51e1d37284d349a29316fd9cc33b0ab3553e7c7c9e1202efa208442e1`\n39\t- browser product owner: `52cfb4f0378d616c11b2aa46ced177d073b691b3120b3c6876363143405b25fe`\n40\t\n41\t## One-off Fable advisory\n42\t\n43\tThe expressly authorized parallel Fable 5.1/high session `a07b9681-5de2-4cb2-a106-ba421f2738c8` finished normally, made no repository changes, and spawned no subagents. It returned no P0 and confirmed the selected fixed-creator checkpoint plus immediate predecessor rollback pair plus external freshness floor. Its two P1s are prospective D.110c-a/b/0b1 gate clarifications: assert closure membership through the inspected advance predicates rather than freezing exact ref arrays, and prove reclamation cannot delete the floor member while cold open still requires it. They do not reopen or widen 0b0. Transcript SHA-256: `65aadcf527dfe334aab9dd9de85489ae2b6690d2def010d24b75f8581b96a6e4`; report SHA-256: `66c8b3a091cd846c11cf46365928322d15832ae007b6347b0cb9fc3250217849`.\n44\t\n45\t## Preserved state and remaining ownership\n46\t\n47\t- Protected `.agents`, `.claude`, and `.pnpm-store` roots are present; 27 stashes are preserved.\n48\t- The browser model provider demonstrates the public capability contract but is not anti-rollback evidence for IndexedDB or another same-storage implementation.\n49\t- D.110c-a/b generalize the same publication law to genuine repeated transitions. D.110c-0b1 owns the bounded epoch-N opener and closure retirement. D.110c-c/d own reclamation, census, restart, and the at-least-100-transition proof. Phase 7 owns external pin delivery and archive/cold-join availability."}
