cannot be re-created; and no silent migration occurs\\\" — none of these is asserted, and the model providers actively re-create the scope on every session because their memory is per-session.\",\n      \"required_fix\": \"Cover the `reopen` initialization kind (absent scope → `D110C_FLOOR_MIGRATION_REQUIRED`), a used-scope re-create returning `conflict` → `D110C_FLOOR_CONFLICT`, and a migrate whose head is cross-object or ahead → `D110C_FLOOR_INVALID`/`_HEAD_AHEAD`, using a provider double whose scope memory persists across sessions.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"p2\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"All pending-recovery failure kinds collapse into an availability code\",\n      \"evidence\": \"examples/v3-room/src/index.ts:2182-2189 maps every `recoveredPending.ok !== true` to `D110C_FLOOR_RECOVERY_UNAVAILABLE`, so the Node owner's `true-fork`, `chain-invalid`, `stale-head` and `pending-old` (packages/node/src/creator-adoption.ts:1365,1393,1413,1426) are reported as availability rather than authority failures, contrary to the frozen table's availability/authority split.\",\n      \"disposition\": \"Map integrity kinds to `D110C_FLOOR_PENDING_INVALID` and reserve `_RECOVERY_UNAVAILABLE` for absent/unavailable selected generations, or record the intentional collapse in the plan's classification table.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Hot activation with an absent floor returns malformed-input, not the frozen floor code\",\n      \"evidence\": \"packages/node/src/creator-adoption-activate.ts:63-79 `capture` requires an exact key set, so a hot `activateCreatorSuccessorAdoption` call omitting `expectedRoomHead` fails at line 240 as `malformed-input`; only the cold path has the explicit `!(\\\"expectedRoomHead\\\" in input)` pre-check at :260-270. `D110C_FLOOR_MIGRATION_REQUIRED` was nevertheless added to the shared roster at tests/fixtures/phase-6a-v3/creator-successor-activation-contract.ts:114-116.\",\n      \"disposition\": \"Either add the same explicit pre-check to the hot